  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Common WASH Pipeline Support across Borno, Adamawa and Yobe States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian response in North-east Nigeria continues to be the most protracted crisis in the humanitarian landscape. IOM remains a key player in the water, sanitation and hygiene sector (WASH) to ensure camps, camp-like settings, and host communities benefit from not only the minimum Sphere requirements but also uninterrupted delivery of these services. This project aims to respond to the emerging needs and gaps as identified by the WASH Sector. IOM through the implementation of this project is complementing existing activities that support rainy season preparedness and response that includes cholera preparedness and response as a key activity. The main activity is creating access to WASH common supplies through IOM&apos;s common supply unit. This aims to ensure beneficiaries have access to various WASH non-food item kits that include menstrual hygiene management kits, replenishment kits, and cholera and sanitation kits.</narrative>
  </description>
